{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"enunciable-paganist-chevrotain","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while implementing 03ef-6fb5-158b-4abd (scheduled mirror main CI).\n\n## Context\n\nBefore 03ef, `codeql.yml` ran on every push to `main` PLUS a weekly schedule, and its own\ncomment described the weekly cron as catching \"advisories that land between pushes\" — i.e. the\npush trigger was the primary scan of new code and the schedule was the backstop for newly\npublished advisories.\n\n03ef dropped the push trigger from every workflow so the mirror's `main` CI reports branch\nhealth on a schedule rather than per-commit. CodeQL was deliberately NOT moved onto the new\n6-hourly tick: it is a security scanner whose cadence is a cost/coverage choice, and 6-hourly\nwould have been a 28x frequency increase nobody asked for. That was the operator's explicit\nreading and it is what shipped.\n\n## The residual question\n\nThe weekly cron is now CodeQL's PRIMARY scan of newly-landed code, not a backstop. Worst case,\na newly-introduced SAST finding sits unscanned for up to 7 days. That may be perfectly\nacceptable — Gerrit's per-patchset gate already runs gitleaks and pip-audit, and CodeQL is an\nindependent layer rather than a merge gate — but the cadence was chosen under different\nassumptions and should be re-decided deliberately rather than inherited by accident.\n\n## What to decide\n\nWhether to leave CodeQL weekly, move it to daily (a modest increase that keeps the scanner\nwell below the branch-health tick), or add a narrower trigger. Note `workflow_dispatch` was\nadded by 03ef, so an on-demand scan after a security-relevant change is already possible today.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The cadence question is decided explicitly, with the reasoning recorded.\n- [ ] If the cadence changes, `.github/workflows/codeql.yml` is updated and its header comment\n      states the new rationale.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py` (which pins codeql's cron and asserts it carries\n      no 6-hourly cron) is updated to match whatever is decided.\n","id":"34b5-ad7d-b983-47f9","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Decide whether CodeQL's weekly cadence is still right now that it no longer runs on push to main"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785957922659459001,"uuid":"b14b34be-e7c8-4307-8e4a-b7b472bf6a2b"}